From: Garnet RDNA4 Darwin <garnet@local>
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] radv/darwin: use ABI 1.14 WebKit-silent APP selector aliases on GarnetAccelerator

Sync include/darwin/rdna4_native_abi.h with GarnetNativeABI.h ABI 1.14
(reserving selector 29, rdna4n_info.flags bit 7, and seqno bit 61 for
VCN 5.0 ABI 1.15; adding WebKit-silent APP aliases 30/31/39 for
BOCREATE/BO_IMPORT_HOST/BUFFER_COPY and info flags bits 8..10).

Route RADV's GarnetAccelerator APP connection through selectors 30/31/39
when the kernel reports ABI minor >= 14, falling back automatically to
legacy selectors 3/21/27 on ABI <= 13 kernels and on the GarnetDriver route.
---
--- a/include/darwin/rdna4_native_abi.h
+++ b/include/darwin/rdna4_native_abi.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 #define RDNA4N_UC_TYPE       0x47524E54u      /* 'GRNT' */
 #define RDNA4N_ABI_VERSION   1u            /* the MAJOR: unchanged, so every v1.0 client (Mesa, rdna4native, s1d-replay) still handshakes */
-#define RDNA4N_ABI_MINOR     13u           /* 1.13: GFX12 Sparse/PRT VM support (RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT in rdna4n_info.flags; RDNA4N_VA_OP_CLEAR, RDNA4N_VA_OP_REPLACE, and RDNA4N_VM_PAGE_PRT with handle == 0; no new selector, no struct size changes). 1.12 (kext 0.0.662, M6 Stage 2): selectors 22..26 also accept INSTANCE 1. 1.11 (kext 0.0.661, M6 Stage 1b): selectors 22..26 RDNA4N_SEL_SCANX_* - the scanout of INSTANCE 2 (the monitor B: HUBP2 / OTG2), poll-only, behind the boot-args garnet-m6=1 AND garnet-m6flip=1 (a latch OFF answers every one with Unsupported and touches nothing); RDNA4N_SCANQ_M6FLIP in scan_query.flags says both are on; no struct changes. 1.10 (kext 0.0.640, GPU-apps G4): rdna4n_info.reserved[3..7] report the session's VRAM budget (RDNA4N_INFO_R_* / RDNA4N_BUDGET_* below), so a user-space allocator (Mesa/RADV) can size its VRAM heap; no selector, no struct size changes. A third client role (APP, a non-root uid >= 501 process on the kernel allow-list) exists behind the boot-args garnet-apps=1 + garnet-multisession=1: it reaches selectors 0, 1, 3..8 and 21 only (never ReadRegs 2, never scanout 9..14, never 15..20); a refused selector is kIOReturnNotPrivileged. 1.9 (kext 0.0.612): selector 21 RDNA4N_SEL_BO_IMPORT_HOST (milestone #11 step 11c: import a page-aligned range of the CALLER's address space as a SYSTEM-memory BO; limits 64 MiB per BO, 256 MiB per client), the class of the RDNA4N user client is renamed IOAccelGarnetNativeClient (WindowServer's sandbox admits iokit-open only for IOAccel* classes; the service name and type 'GRNT' are unchanged), and a uid-88 caller is admitted behind the boot-arg garnet-metal-ws=1; 1.8 (kext 0.0.610): selectors 19 RDNA4N_SEL_METAL_NUB_PUBLISH and 20 RDNA4N_SEL_METAL_NUB_WITHDRAW (milestone #9 route A: the software GarnetMetalNub the aux accelerator kext matches; published only on demand, only with the boot-arg garnet-metal=1); 1.7 (kext 0.0.609): HELD mode for row 120: selector 17 RDNA4N_SEL_MODE_HOLD (enter row 120 and RETURN with the mode up, a scanout client may then Acquire and present at 120 Hz) and selector 18 RDNA4N_SEL_MODE_RELEASE (end it, wait, return the final result); verdict 16 HELD, deny 25 / 26, RDNA4N_HOLD_* words; the result's former reserved0 / reserved1 (offsets 204 / 252) are hold_end / hold_flags (the size stays 512 B); 1.6 (kext 0.0.608): row 120's blanked-transition underflow reads, DIO attribution and lock-hold witness code in the result's former reserved[8] (the size stays 512 B); 1.5 (kext 0.0.607): row 120 (the 1440p 120 Hz trial) runs behind the boot-arg garnet-row120=1 with the clock hold (P4); the result's ext.reserved words carry the hold report (its size is unchanged); new deny reasons 22 / 23, verdict 15, flags 22..24; 1.4 (kext 0.0.606): selector 16's result grows from 256 to 512 B (underflow / resync / OTG-lock report) and it accepts the rows 1 (DP1 resync) and 2 (V_TOTAL under the OTG lock) and a flags word; 1.3 (kext 0.0.605): the timed mode-trial selector 16, native-S2d; 1.2 (kext 0.0.604): the DAL experiment selector 15, native-S2-DISPCLK; 1.1 (kext 0.0.603): the scanout selectors 9..14, native-S2a. Reported when Hello asks (below) and in rdna4n_info.reserved[2]. */
+#define RDNA4N_ABI_MINOR     14u           /* 1.14: WebKit-silent APP selector aliases 30 (BOCREATE), 31 (BO_IMPORT_HOST), 39 (BUFFER_COPY) and kernel-authoritative rdna4n_info.flags bits 8..10 (READY, DISPLAY_ACTIVE, KILL_SWITCH); reserves selector 29, flags bit 7, and seqno bit 61 for VCN 5.0 (ABI 1.15). 1.13: GFX12 Sparse/PRT VM support (RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT in rdna4n_info.flags; RDNA4N_VA_OP_CLEAR, RDNA4N_VA_OP_REPLACE, and RDNA4N_VM_PAGE_PRT with handle == 0; no new selector, no struct size changes). 1.12 (kext 0.0.662, M6 Stage 2): selectors 22..26 also accept INSTANCE 1. 1.11 (kext 0.0.661, M6 Stage 1b): selectors 22..26 RDNA4N_SEL_SCANX_* - the scanout of INSTANCE 2 (the monitor B: HUBP2 / OTG2), poll-only, behind the boot-args garnet-m6=1 AND garnet-m6flip=1 (a latch OFF answers every one with Unsupported and touches nothing); RDNA4N_SCANQ_M6FLIP in scan_query.flags says both are on; no struct changes. 1.10 (kext 0.0.640, GPU-apps G4): rdna4n_info.reserved[3..7] report the session's VRAM budget (RDNA4N_INFO_R_* / RDNA4N_BUDGET_* below), so a user-space allocator (Mesa/RADV) can size its VRAM heap; no selector, no struct size changes. A third client role (APP, a non-root uid >= 501 process on the kernel allow-list) exists behind the boot-args garnet-apps=1 + garnet-multisession=1: it reaches selectors 0, 1, 3..8 and 21 only (never ReadRegs 2, never scanout 9..14, never 15..20); a refused selector is kIOReturnNotPrivileged. 1.9 (kext 0.0.612): selector 21 RDNA4N_SEL_BO_IMPORT_HOST (milestone #11 step 11c: import a page-aligned range of the CALLER's address space as a SYSTEM-memory BO; limits 64 MiB per BO, 256 MiB per client), the class of the RDNA4N user client is renamed IOAccelGarnetNativeClient (WindowServer's sandbox admits iokit-open only for IOAccel* classes; the service name and type 'GRNT' are unchanged), and a uid-88 caller is admitted behind the boot-arg garnet-metal-ws=1; 1.8 (kext 0.0.610): selectors 19 RDNA4N_SEL_METAL_NUB_PUBLISH and 20 RDNA4N_SEL_METAL_NUB_WITHDRAW (milestone #9 route A: the software GarnetMetalNub the aux accelerator kext matches; published only on demand, only with the boot-arg garnet-metal=1); 1.7 (kext 0.0.609): HELD mode for row 120: selector 17 RDNA4N_SEL_MODE_HOLD (enter row 120 and RETURN with the mode up, a scanout client may then Acquire and present at 120 Hz) and selector 18 RDNA4N_SEL_MODE_RELEASE (end it, wait, return the final result); verdict 16 HELD, deny 25 / 26, RDNA4N_HOLD_* words; the result's former reserved0 / reserved1 (offsets 204 / 252) are hold_end / hold_flags (the size stays 512 B); 1.6 (kext 0.0.608): row 120's blanked-transition underflow reads, DIO attribution and lock-hold witness code in the result's former reserved[8] (the size stays 512 B); 1.5 (kext 0.0.607): row 120 (the 1440p 120 Hz trial) runs behind the boot-arg garnet-row120=1 with the clock hold (P4); the result's ext.reserved words carry the hold report (its size is unchanged); new deny reasons 22 / 23, verdict 15, flags 22..24; 1.4 (kext 0.0.606): selector 16's result grows from 256 to 512 B (underflow / resync / OTG-lock report) and it accepts the rows 1 (DP1 resync) and 2 (V_TOTAL under the OTG lock) and a flags word; 1.3 (kext 0.0.605): the timed mode-trial selector 16, native-S2d; 1.2 (kext 0.0.604): the DAL experiment selector 15, native-S2-DISPCLK; 1.1 (kext 0.0.603): the scanout selectors 9..14, native-S2a. Reported when Hello asks (below) and in rdna4n_info.reserved[2]. */
 #define RDNA4N_HELLO_F_MINOR (1u << 8)     /* Hello flags bit 8: "report the minor": out[0] = ABI | (MINOR << 16). Without it out[0] is exactly the major, as in v1.0. Bit 8, not 0: flags = 1, which T1 leg 1 sends and expects refused, still is. */
 #define RDNA4N_MAX_IBS       64u
 #define RDNA4N_MAX_BOS       4096u            /* handles 1..4095; 0 is never valid */
